<div id="2026-11-17-i18n-catalog-p0" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-17 — I18N-CATALOG Phase 0: per-user display language preference</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The catalog keeps ONE stored language and is now displayed in each user's own language. Phase 0 adds the storage and the resolver: the <code>ui.language</code> key in <code>user_preferences</code> (with a shape check so <code>xx</code>/<code>french</code>/<code>fr2</code> are rejected rather than normalised to <code>en</code>, <code>fr-CA</code> stored as <code>fr</code>, and an empty value deleting the row), plus the new <code>Comserv::Util::UserLanguage</code> resolver (<code>current</code>, <code>preference</code>, <code>catalog_language</code>, <code>translation_active</code>, <code>supported_languages</code>) memoised in the stash. <code>Comserv::Util::TextTranslate</code> gained <code>is_supported</code> and <code>languages</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Display-time translation needs a target language per user, and the catalog must never fork per user — a second stored language breaks barcode matching. No schema change was needed: <code>user_preferences</code>, its whitelist and the <code>/user/prefs</code> endpoint already exist and are used by <code>ui.theme_override</code>/<code>ui.timezone</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Translation quality (amended 2026-11-17).</strong> A model can return a fluent, plausible and wrong string and nothing in the app can tell. The plan now treats a translation as a claim: Phase 1 adds write-time guards (<code>Comserv::Util::TranslationGuard</code> — glossary conformance, token/unit preservation, echo/unchanged reply, script sanity, length-ratio bound) that log and refuse a bad candidate instead of caching it and fall back to the stored text; Phase 5 adds a report affordance, a review queue sorted by <code>hit_count</code>, approve/reject and purge-on-reject. The cache spec grew <code>quality</code>/<code>reviewed_at</code>/<code>reviewed_by</code>/<code>rejected_reason</code> plus a <code>translation_flag</code> table, so the schema hand-off (schema todo #2756) was amended to rev 2 before that branch starts.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/UserLanguage.pm</code> (new), <code>lib/Comserv/Util/UserPreferences.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/TextTranslate.pm</code>, <code>t/i18n_user_language.t</code> (new, 31 tests), <code>root/Documentation/system/i18n_catalog_language_plan.tt</code> (new plan, project #313 I18N-CATALOG), <code>script/sync_ai_plan_to_projects.pl</code> (UTF-8 read + no description bleed past the last phase).</p>
</div>
